{
  "findings": [
    "Fixed relative-target lookup improves throughput but remains below real time.",
    "User-initiated QoS/activity provided no meaningful benefit; before the diagnostic change the main thread was already user-interactive. Original QoS was restored.",
    "No native fault or audio-engine initialization failure in these runs; undersupply and clock gaps remain unresolved.",
    "Combined straight-line game/BIOS blocks reached0.97527 emulated seconds per wall second, with40 underruns and10 clock gaps: still unqualified.",
    "The separately instrumented combined candidate had45 underruns;44 coincided with native-call duration exceeding that call\u2019s emulated interval. Swift picture/PCM copies were about0.1ms in the slow gameplay section.",
    "A single instrumented backlog followed audio recovery and legitimate simulation catch-up; all4659 enqueue totals balanced. It is not evidence of duplicate PCM or accumulating device sample-rate drift.",
    "Inlining fixed fetch/cycle helpers and exactly repeating the measured delayed-branch loop improved the latest ratio to 0.988315, but 18 underruns, one backlog and five clock gaps remain; CPU optimization is still in progress.",
    "Repeating the second measured self-loop reached 0.989715 with 13 underruns and four clock gaps. Startup no longer discarded time in this run; all four gaps occurred in the short gameplay section. This candidate remains unqualified.",
    "Five guarded delay-slot specializations preserved exact output but did not eliminate the slow gameplay section: the clean four-delay candidate still had 13 underruns and four clock gaps at 0.989544. A new profile is required before choosing further changes.",
    "Guarded mapped instruction fetch passed independent memory tests and the full replay. Its clean playback run completed startup without underflow or time loss, but the gameplay phase still caused 11 underruns, one backlog and three clock gaps; ratio 0.991377.",
    "A six-node guarded inline chain preserved exact output and all focused CPU/memory tests, but the clean 120-second run still had 11 underruns and four clock gaps during gameplay at ratio 0.990630. Startup remained clean. This candidate is not qualified for promotion.",
    "Block/chain-only mapped read32 passed 78,024 independent data-read cases and all existing CPU/memory/replay proofs, but clean playback still failed: 0.992473 ratio, 11 underruns, one backlog and three clock gaps. Further CPU work remains.",
    "Post-fetch-PC hardening, direct-label chain control flow and three exact MOV.L inline annotations passed strengthened CPU proofs and full replay equality, but clean playback remains unqualified: 0.992193 ratio, 11 underruns, one backlog and three gaps. Repeated dispatch-only refinements have not resolved the local CPU deficit.",
    "A narrowly guarded native counter-loop contraction passed full replay equality and 4,278 independent mapped-RAM cases, including 450 actual interrupt deliveries. Clean playback improved to 0.996770 with five underruns (one startup, four gameplay), no backlog recovery and one clock gap. The same short gameplay section still needs CPU headroom; this is not a real-time acceptance. Successful batching intentionally elides unobservable ordinary RAM access events while preserving complete CPU/cycle/RAM state at the admitted boundaries.",
    "Combining the telemetry-free data-first counter helper with the independently qualified direct-PC ARM7 lookup reduced main-thread update work to85.786s across120s, but the same gameplay phase still caused four underruns and one clock gap. Startup was clean. No clock/audio thresholds were changed; real-time qualification remains incomplete.",
    "Adding128 phase-selected ordinary fixed blocks preserved all6,244 original replay rows and passed166,951 block comparisons plus16,772 rejection checks, but live playback still had four underruns and one discarded clock gap (0.996942 ratio). The additional blocks did not establish a meaningful live improvement and remain experimental.",
    "A scene-owned continuation experiment reduced unnecessary idle and retained elapsed game time, but remained unqualified: three underruns, one backlog recovery and0.998855 timing ratio. Its zero gap counter was misleading because end-of-callback debt omitted current CPU work; trace measured324ms actual lag. Chained CoreFoundation blocks also delayed a display-timer callback by771ms. Next scheduling work must account elapsed CPU time at chunk exit and bound event-loop fairness, while preserving the250ms limits.",
    "One-shot main-run-loop timers and one native step per chunk fixed the earlier timer-starvation issue. End-of-chunk accounting now includes all CPU time before enforcing the original250ms limit. With grouped guards and reordered native functions,90s playback still had three underruns and one discarded gap; this is not a pass.",
    "Restricting texture creation to external display callbacks preserves the latest completed native image while avoiding unseen uploads. In the same-engine90s comparison, scene work decreased from63.509s to62.770s and underruns from three to two, but one clock gap remained. All original CPU steps, PCM batches and clock limits remained unchanged."
  ],
